(function(r){r.locales.en=Object.freeze({...r.locales.en,"guide.contents":"Guide contents","guide.start":"Getting started","guide.startText":"Extract the entire folder and open index.html in a tested desktop browser. No Internet, server or tool installation is needed. This version is still in development: use fictional data.\n\nCreate an organization or restore a full backup from Backups. Choose language, currency and time zone; currency cannot change once financial movements exist. The toolbar language changes the interface, not names or notes you entered.","guide.settings":"Settings","guide.settingsText":"Set the organization name, print details and footer, logo, animal preferences and backup reminders. Reminders run while the application is open; they do not create backups.\n\nManage catalogs and locations in Settings. Deactivating an option prevents new selections while preserving historical references. Review dependencies before archiving or removing records.","guide.animals":"Animals and history","guide.animalsText":"Create the profile and entry with a date, location and availability. Leave the code empty for automatic assignment; an assigned code keeps its identity. Values within one filter combine with OR; different filters combine with AND.\n\nThe profile brings together episodes, foster stays, adoptions, health, tasks, documents, photos and weights. Use the appropriate transition for transfers, exits, death or reentry. A return opens another episode. History opens the source record and offers date corrections for supported facts. Review the date, reason and each related closure before confirming. Original events remain available; correcting a date does not reverse a state or repeat money, stock or clinical actions.","guide.contacts":"Contacts and volunteering","guide.contactsText":"Keep one contact per person, with multiple roles when needed. Store phones, emails and notes; create foster or volunteer profiles on the existing contact.\n\nReview matches and compare before confirming a merge. An identical name alone does not establish identity. Volunteer profiles record activities and minutes; totals are derived by period without creating another contact.","guide.health":"Health and care","guide.healthText":"Record performed procedures, active conditions and care plans from the animal profile. The application stores instructions provided by the person or veterinary professional; it does not calculate doses or recommend treatments.\n\nA planned clinical task is not a performed procedure. Complete it through the health workflow to preserve the link. For an expense, choose a new movement or an existing invoice: do not enter the same expense again in Finance.","guide.fosters":"Foster care","guide.fostersText":"Create a foster profile on a contact, with capacity and restrictions. Assign animals through the foster workflow and review occupancy, compatibility and any explicit exception.\n\nEnd a stay with its date and destination. Ending a foster stay alone does not record an adoption or final shelter exit. Keep ended stays as history.","guide.adoptions":"Adoptions and returns","guide.adoptionsText":"Link the application, contact and animal. Review, approve and reserve when appropriate; each step has its dates and reasons. Finalize through Adoptions and explicitly decide what happens to pending tasks. An optional fee creates one income movement.\n\nA return preserves the earlier adoption and opens a new entry. Do not delete an adoption to represent a return. The global register filters applications, reservations and adoptions by their own dates and states.","guide.tasks":"Tasks and calendar","guide.tasksText":"The list and calendar show the same tasks. Use calendar dates and, where appropriate, a time and time zone. An overdue task remains pending until completed or cancelled. Opening the calendar does not perform procedures or send notifications outside the application.\n\nComplete clinical tasks through their health workflow. When closing an adoption, exit or plan, review each pending task; do not assume they are all cancelled automatically.","guide.finance":"Finance","guide.financeText":"Record independent income and expenses with a date, category and exact amount in the organization currency. Amounts are stored as integer minor units. Totals depend on the visible period and filters.\n\nRecord donations, adoption fees, stock purchases and clinical expenses through their own modules to retain their source. A financial correction creates a linked replacement and voids the original with a reason; it does not overwrite the historical amount. Review its effect before confirming.","guide.donations":"Donations","guide.donationsText":"A monetary donation records exactly one linked income movement. A material donation groups lines by type, unit and quantity; each line can enter inventory. An estimated material value is not income received.\n\nVoiding coordinates the income or stock effects. Do not compensate a material line already voided, or add another stock receipt for a donation that already created it.","guide.inventory":"Inventory","guide.inventoryText":"Create items with a unit, precision and minimum. Stock is derived from opening balances, purchases, donations, consumption, returns and adjustments. Use quantities compatible with the item precision.\n\nA purchase can record its expense once. Correct movements through compensation and review historical balances: the application rejects negative stock at any point. A minimum is an indicator, not an automatic purchase.","guide.documents":"Documents and photos","guide.documentsText":"An embedded document stores bytes in the browser and full backup; an external reference stores metadata and an optional hash, without the original file. Transfer those originals separately and select them again to compare identity.\n\nLink documents to their source records. Images are validated and resized with a thumbnail. Downloading a document verifies its bytes. The application file budget includes archived and trashed assets. To change an existing document date, use its dedicated correction action and review all linked animal histories. File bytes and links are preserved.","guide.exchange":"Import and export","guide.exchangeText":"CSV supports contacts, animals, volunteer profiles, applications, financial movements and donations. Select delimiter, date and amount interpretation, map columns and review every identity or conflict. Grouped material lines succeed or fail together. Only an explicitly confirmed subset is applied.\n\nModule JSON preserves types and relationships. It contains no bytes: select the requested files to verify their hashes. Review links and profile changes; it does not overwrite financial or historical facts. Resolve missing references before applying. A partial export does not replace a full backup.","guide.backup":"Backup, verification and restoration","guide.backupText":"In Backups, generate and download the full file. Select that downloaded file again to verify it; downloading alone does not establish that it was retained correctly. Keep dated external copies and protect their contents. Complex changes require a verified backup of the current revision.\n\nRestoration replaces the active organization through separate preparation and atomic activation. Review organization, date, counts and files before confirming. Cancellation is possible only before activation. Previous datasets and interrupted preparations are listed for recovery; they are not external backups and are not automatically cleaned up.","guide.transfer":"Changing browser or computer","guide.transferText":"On the original computer, generate, download and select a full backup again to verify it. Keep the file outside browser storage. Also transfer original external documents and the complete application folder.\n\nAt the destination, extract and open index.html, select Restore and review the backup before confirming. Check animals, totals and files afterwards. Another profile, browser or location may use different storage. Keep the original data until the destination is checked. Copying HTML or cloning Git does not transfer IndexedDB.","guide.update":"Updating safely","guide.updateText":"Before updating, create and verify an external backup and temporarily keep the previous application folder. Close other application tabs, extract the complete new version and open its index.html.\n\nCheck the organization, counts and documents after supported migrations. If a different storage location shows an empty organization, restore the verified backup; do not recreate duplicate records. Do not open a migrated database with an older version or force a future-version backup. Keeping old application files does not reverse a browser database migration.","guide.trash":"Archive and trash","guide.trashText":"Archiving and trash preserve records and relationships; they are not permanent deletion and do not automatically release bytes. Use the module archive/trash filters and restore action.\n\nThe application blocks removal of animals under care or with pending tasks and protects other dependencies. Resolve the corresponding business event instead of deleting references. Storage lets you review and permanently remove one inactive recovery dataset or interrupted preparation. Verify a current external backup first; a recovery dataset also needs its own verified external file and explicit confirmation that you retain it. Removing it loses that local recovery option. Each removal records activity, so verify a new current copy before removing another. Permanent business-record deletion, unused active-file cleanup and automatic retention remain pending.","guide.troubleshoot":"Troubleshooting","guide.troubleshootText":"If data seems missing, check the browser, profile, location and private mode. Do not clear storage to fix it. Preserve the original profile data and transfer using a verified external backup.\n\nOnly one tab controls writes. After reloading it can take about 15 seconds to regain control; close old tabs and retry. If a revision changed, review the form again using current data. For quota or unavailable storage, keep external backups and free computer space; temporary memory is not used as a save fallback. Future versions or incorrect hashes are rejected: do not edit the JSON to bypass validation.","guide.demo":"Exploring and removing the demonstration","guide.demoText":"In Demonstration, load EN/ES examples only in an organization without real business data or another demo batch. Review the plan, verify a current backup and confirm. Examples never load on opening. Dates are relative to the loading day and all content is fictional.\n\nNew work you enter is real. Removing a batch detects real references and offers to retain connected examples as real with additional consent, while removing the rest. Review fictional names and amounts before operational use. Do not use restoration as a delete-examples button."});}(window.RescueManager));

